# 9router_WatchEdit repository hygiene
# NOTE: .gitignore is NOT a security boundary. Secrets must physically live
# outside the repository (see SECURITY_LOCAL.md). These rules only reduce
# accidents; the pre-commit hook and safe-share scanner provide the gates.

# --- Private / secret-bearing material (must NEVER exist in this repo) ---
backup/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
jwt-secret
machine-id
.env
.env.*
*.vault
*.partial
credentials.json
providers-state-export.json
*.dpapi

# --- Local runtime state (belongs in %LOCALAPPDATA%\9router_WatchEdit) ---
health_cache.json
presets.json
settings.json
*.log
logs/

# --- Engine release artifacts (kept on disk, never committed) ---
packages/
patches/

# --- Python / tooling ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Agent / editor state (IDENTITY.md is the portable lineage carrier and
#      must stay tracked; everything else under .saipen/ is local state) ---
.saipen/*
!.saipen/IDENTITY.md
# --- Release surface: the translation kitchen's verified locale READMEs are
#      part of the release contract (the ship gate requires every one of them
#      staged and committed so a fresh clone exposes them), so they must be
#      trackable even though the rest of .saipen/ is local state. Only the
#      surfaces themselves -- no cache, no scratch, no state. ---
!.saipen/saitranslate/
.saipen/saitranslate/*
!.saipen/saitranslate/kitchen/
.saipen/saitranslate/kitchen/*
!.saipen/saitranslate/kitchen/*/
!.saipen/saitranslate/kitchen/*/README_*.md
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Live provider/runtime caches (fetched data, never source) ---
.freebuff/

# --- Node tooling deps (the WatchEdit app is Python; node_modules only
#      holds the ad-hoc vitest cache used by the 9router build helper) ---
node_modules/
